module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.docs_markdown_projections_have_no_completing_actuator

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data docs_markdown_projections_have_no_completing_actuator: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "docs_markdown_projections_have_no_completing_actuator" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**generated `docs/*.md` ledger projections have no ProcessExit actuator and no regen coverage, so an EDIT to a still-present row can sit in the authority, absent from the projection, with every completing instrument green** (INVALID STATE: `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` is the authority; `docs/design-failure-modes.md` is the projection DESIGN.md points readers at. `expected_design_failure_modes_md` returns `String`. The refusal exits 2 with EMPTY STDOUT and interpolates the rendered value into the diagnostic on stderr: classify_exit's non-variant arm is type_name: ctx.format_value(other). Executed: wise-badger-902, EXIT=2, stdout 0 bytes, stderr 578588 bytes opening with the markdown heading; quick-heron-85, proj3.err 1062137 bytes, same delimiters. The enrolled control `non_process_exit_refuses_rather_than_printing_and_succeeding` forbids print-AND-SUCCEED, and holds. The content is therefore obtainable ONLY by scraping a half-megabyte stderr diagnostic between delimiters that are message prose (returned-open-quote and not-ProcessExit-close-quote), unversioned and enrolled by nothing. Extractable only by scraping an unversioned diagnostic — which is why the ProcessExit regen is the repair. `claim_executor --required-regen` compares only `is_compared_generated_basename` = ends_with .rs into `target/stage0-regen-candidate`. HARM: three rows can be edited in `.dag` after the last projection and nothing that exits 0 will say the markdown is stale. The meaning-fork in the field named type_name is a separate row, `type_name_field_carries_rendered_value`, not this class.",

    "SPECIMEN, measured by another lane while regenerating the projection, 2026-09-06: `instrument_answers_outside_its_domain`, `stale_claim_survives_its_own_correct_edit`, and `native_stack_recursion_unbounded_over_corpus_shaped_structure` had been edited in their authorities after the doc was last projected and had grown by 2349, 5519 and 1152 characters. Regenerating carried the repairs through. On origin/main as of 3531d30bb82 those three `.dag` files are older than `docs/design-failure-modes.md` (`81686f7bea8`), so CURRENT main is not claimed still stale; the class is that nothing completing could have said so while they were.",

    "SPECIMEN, review 58567 on gunbc#9864, on the host comment above `exit_status_for_class`: a relocation dropped the `status: refused — printing the value and exiting 0 would report success for a run whose outcome is unknown.` sentence while the comment claimed byte-for-byte equivalence. The doc lied, not the code. The sentence was restored rather than the claim weakened. That is this class on a different pair: an authority and its projection disagreeing with nothing completing to say so, and a real specimen rather than an injected literal.",

    "INCIDENT, not a fixture and not a perturbation ordered for this PR, produced by quick-heron-85 without looking for this class, commit b1c6378c6d: their authority row unresolved_callee_conflated_with_dispatched_elsewhere was UNPARSEABLE for a full commit. An authored receipt contained a quoted phrase using bare double quotes inside a double-quoted string; the string terminated early and the parser refused undefined variable this and undefined variable leaf. THE AUTHORITY DID NOT COMPILE, so docs/design-failure-modes.md kept rendering the previous vintage while presenting as current. They found it only by running the projection; reading the row does not surface the break. This PR's gate would go red on that commit because an unparseable authority makes the projector refuse — from the committed markdown alone, STALE bytes and an UNBUILDABLE authority are indistinguishable. THIS ROW IS THE DETECTOR GAP. The quoting injury that silently disabled the row they were filing is a neighbouring class they are filing separately; its next-rung trigger is string escaping in the .dag lexer. This gate makes that injury loud; it does not make it unwritable. Do not read this row as closing that class.",

    "THE IDENTITY-JOIN CORRECTION, which is the transferable part and which corrects a rule this project holds. Completeness is an identity join, not a count equality — and AN IDENTITY JOIN OVER ROW NAMES WOULD HAVE REPORTED THAT FILE COMPLETE AND CORRECT: every identity present, none missing, none extra. The drift was pure EDIT. Only a regenerated byte diff sees an edit. Worse: a first pass comparing line SETS read the three as REORDERINGS, because the changed rows shared an 80-character prefix with their old text, so the cheap check does not merely miss the drift, it manufactures a benign explanation for it. An identity join proves MEMBERSHIP, not CONTENT.",

    "THE TWO NEIGHBOURS THIS IS NOT. `authority_merges_unprotected_while_its_projection_is_guarded` is MERGE POLARITY: the generated projection is driver-bound while the hand-authored authority is not. Adjacent files, distinct defect — this row is the absence of a completing actuator or content gate, reachable with no merge in sight. `green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own` is a split of actuators whose GREEN is read as covering the half it does not enumerate; that climb joined registry-projections to stage0-mirrors inside one required phase, and still does not give `gunbc run` a ProcessExit projector for the markdown, nor put `.md` in `--required-regen`.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a generated file is what readers are pointed at, ask (1) whether any `ProcessExit` entry writes those exact bytes and exits 0, (2) whether regen's compared population includes that path, and (3) whether the gate compares CONTENT, not row-name membership. A complete identity set of names is not a content agreement.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder until a completing content agreement exists — silent wrongness, not a weak wall. After a ProcessExit projector and a required content compare execute, mechanically preventable: the stale file remains writable. CEILING: structurally guaranteed when membership of every committed generated `docs/` path in a content-agreement adjudicator is derived from `gunbc.generated_artifact` `committed_generated_artifacts`, so omitting the arm is a compile refusal.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability: required-run dispatch consumes a content agreement — byte identity of generated vs committed — over every committed generated artifact whose location directory is `docs`, derived from the registry so adding a committed `docs/` path without that agreement will not compile. A trigger naming one command, one test file, or `docs_projection_gate.dag` is less than the capability and would fire while edit-only drift can still sit uncompared.)",
    "**THE CLIMB THIS ROW ANTICIPATED HAS EXECUTED, CONFIRMED BY A LANE THAT DID NOT AUTHOR IT, AND THE RESIDUE IS NARROWER THAN THE TRIGGER SENTENCE READS** (warm-stag-726, 2026-09-07). This row and `tools.docs_projection_gate` landed in the same change, so the row's opening INVALID STATE describes the pre-repair state and its rung sentence conditions the climb on a projector and a required content compare both EXECUTING. Both now do, and the pair was measured from the outside rather than asserted: a head carrying four edited `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` rows with the projection unregenerated was REFUSED by `claim_executor --required-ci --required-lane build` at `generated-artifact population=docs-projections`, naming the path and printing the `regen` recipe; running that recipe rewrote exactly the four rendered lines the four edits own; and `main` on the same entry then exited 0 over both ledger paths. RED on the real acceptance path and an accepted positive control, one binary, one tree -- so the class is MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE today and citing it as outside the ladder would now be the stale half of its own first paragraph.",

    "**MEMBERSHIP IS NOW DERIVED, AND THE PARAGRAPH BELOW IS THE STATE THIS ONE REPLACES -- BUT THE TRIGGER IS SATISFIED FOR NEW REGISTRY VARIANTS ONLY, WHICH IS LESS THAN IT READS** (sharp-lark-759, 2026-09-12). The predicted victim arrived: a third committed docs/ projection, docs/onboarding.md from gunbc.contributor_onboarding_path, added by the contributor-onboarding item. Extending the two literals to three would have been the reading the paragraph below forbids by name, so the enumeration was replaced instead. tools.docs_projection_gate now carries docs_projection_producer, a match TOTAL over GeneratedArtifact with NO WILDCARD, and main and regen enumerate nothing: main folds committed_generated_artifacts and regen folds generated_artifact_registry, each filtered on artifact_location directory equal to the docs directory, so a committed docs/ path is enrolled in the content agreement with no edit to either fold. THE ASYMMETRY BETWEEN THE TWO FOLDS IS PRESERVED BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by the comment that used to carry it: the failure-mode ledger is NotCommitted, so it is written by regen and excluded from main by the commit policy, and agreeing it would still be permanently green. WHAT THIS DOES AND DOES NOT REACH, because the trigger says WILL NOT COMPILE and that is true of one of the two ways a docs/ path can appear. Adding a new registry VARIANT does not compile until it is classified in docs_projection_producer, which is the trigger's own standard. Adding a docs/-located path through an ALREADY-PARAMETERIZED variant -- a PlanArtifact whose plan directory is docs is the reachable case -- still compiles, because the variant already has an Absent arm; that state is refused at runtime by docs_projection_producer_coverage, which folds the docs-located population, names every path with no producer and stops the line, so it is loud rather than silent. SO THE RUNG IS MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE AND THE CEILING IS UNCHANGED: the residual class is a docs/-located parameterized artifact, its refusal is a run rather than a compile, and the remaining trigger is the location directory participating in the producer obligation structurally -- a docs/ location that cannot be constructed without a producer -- at which point the coverage fold dissolves with it. Executed on this change: the gate entry compiled with 0 blocking errors, regen wrote the three docs/ projections, and main exited 0 over the committed two; the discriminating arms are enrolled in test.claim.contributor_onboarding_path, including a non-docs artifact that must not enter the docs population and a committed-versus-written population asymmetry that must not collapse.",
    "**WHAT IS NOT DISCHARGED, STATED AT THE GRAIN THE CEILING ASKS FOR: MEMBERSHIP IS TWO HAND-WRITTEN ARMS.** `tools.docs_projection_gate` `main` and `regen` each name `DesignFailureModesArtifact` and `DesignRungDropsArtifact` literally, and `gunbc.generated_artifact` `artifact_location` carries exactly those two rows with `directory: \"docs\"`, so the enumeration is COINCIDENTALLY complete rather than derived. A third committed `docs/` projection added to the registry compiles, ships, and is compared by nothing -- which is this row's own recognition-rule question (2) answered NO for the artifact that does not exist yet. So the trigger stands unweakened and is restated as the one thing still missing: membership derived from `committed_generated_artifacts` so that the omission is a compile refusal, not a second projector, a third arm, or another gate file.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.design_ledgers", decl_name: "expected_design_failure_modes_md", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.required_regen_host", decl_name: "is_compared_generated_basename", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "classify_exit", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1_compiler.cli_run", decl_name: "exit_status_for_class", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
